        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cd16d051-de68-5584-a440-480a416af787",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Neil B. Shulman, Michael Caton-Jones, Jeffrey Price, Peter S. Seaman, Dallas Hall, Elijah Saunders\n- Organizations: International Society on Hypertension in Blacks\n- Products: Doc Hollywood, What?, Ethnicity & Disease\n- Topics: hypertension among African Americans, minority health\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, physicians Dallas Hall, Neil B. Shulman, and Elijah Saunders founded the International Society on Hypertension in Blacks in response to concern about high rates of hypertension among African Americans.\n- In 1991, the film Doc Hollywood was released as an American romantic comedy directed by Michael Caton-Jones and written by Jeffrey Price and Peter S. Seaman.\n- In 1991, Doc Hollywood was based on Neil B. Shulman's book What?, and Neil B. Shulman was the film's associate producer.\n- In 1991, Ethnicity & Disease was established and published by the International Society on Hypertension in Blacks as its official journal.\n- By 2006, the International Society on Hypertension in Blacks had broadened its scope from reducing hypertension among African Americans to improving the health of minority populations around the world.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3d0c9bf9-385f-537e-b17d-10359ad905f4",
        "text": "Page: Neil B. Shulman. Sentence: He is the associate producer of the 1991 film \"Doc Hollywood\", based on one of his books.\nPage: Doc Hollywood. Sentence: Doc Hollywood is a 1991 American romantic comedy film directed by Michael Caton-Jones, and written by Jeffrey Price and Peter S. Seaman, based on Neil B. Shulman's book, \"What?\nPage: International Society on Hypertension in Blacks. Sentence: It was founded in 1986 by the physicians Dallas Hall, Neil B. Shulman, and Elijah Saunders, in response to concern about high rates of hypertension among African Americans. By 2006, the society had broadened its scope to focus not just on reducing rates of hypertension among African Americans, but also on improving the health of all minority populations around the world.\nPage: Ethnicity &amp; Disease. Sentence: It was established in 1991 and is published by the International Society on Hypertension in Blacks, of which it is the official journal.",
